      "id": "CORE-PIPE-TRACE-01",
      "title": "At TRACE level the same transformation failure is caught and the raw value passes through",
      "tier": "core",
      "intent": "The counterpart of CORE-PIPE-WEDGE-01's transformation trigger, run with -trace (cliLogLevel; the CLI level overrides the config LogLevel, MainControllerService.kt:485). At TRACE level ScheduleReader runs the transformation synchronously inside the try (ScheduleReader.kt:714-726), so the TransformationException is caught, 'Error applying transformation \"RT\"' is logged and the untransformed value is kept. The identical configuration that produces zero Xform records at -info therefore produces a record per read here, carrying the raw bytes [18, 52]: error containment depends on the log level.",
      "pins": [
        "core/sfc-main/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/ScheduleReader.kt:714-726",
        "core/sfc-main/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/MainControllerService.kt:485"
      ],
      "timeoutSeconds": 90,
      "modeParity": false,
      "cliLogLevel": "trace",
      "sinks": {
        "main": {},
        "ctl": {}
      },
      "gates": [
        {
          "sink": "ctl",
          "records": 30
        },
        {
          "sink": "main",
          "records": 10
        }
      ],
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "recordCount",
          "sink": "main",
          "min": 10
        },
        {
          "kind": "channelSequence",
          "sink": "main",
          "source": "srcXf",
          "channel": "clean",
          "step": 1
        },
        {
          "kind": "everyRecord",
          "sink": "main",
          "path": "sources.srcXf.values.pair.value",
          "equals": [
            18,
            52
          ],
          "strictTypes": true,
          "comment": "raw, untransformed"
        },
        {
          "kind": "logContains",
          "text": "Error applying transformation \"RT\""
        },
        {
          "kind": "logAbsent",
          "texts": [
            "Error processing data from reader"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "priority": "P2",
      "config": {
        "AWSVersion": "2022-04-02",
        "Name": "CORE-PIPE-TRACE-01",
        "Version": 1,
        "LogLevel": "Info",
        "Transformations": {
